% M7-T7, the degenerate half: a search array of NOTHING BUT CONSTANTS, inside a
% `seq_search`. The flattener produces this whenever every variable an `int_search`
% named turned out to be fixed -- and before M7-T7 it refused the model.
%
% The phase is empty, which is legal rather than an error: `Search.sequence` skips any
% phase with no unfixed candidate, so this one contributes no decision and the NEXT
% phase is consulted. That second phase is what actually chooses here, and it chooses
% indomain_max, so the answer pins which phase ran: b is searched high-first and the
% only solution with a + b <= 4 and b >= a + 1 that indomain_max reaches first is
% b = 3, a = 1. Had the empty phase swallowed the sequence and fallen back to
% docs/SPEC.md 3.4's default (first-fail, indomain_min) the answer would be a = 1,
% b = 2 instead, so this model tells the two apart.
var 1..3: a :: output_var;
var 1..3: b :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_le([1, 1], [a, b], 4);
constraint int_lin_le([1, -1], [a, b], -1);
solve :: seq_search([int_search([1, 2], input_order, indomain_min, complete),
                     int_search([b, a], input_order, indomain_max, complete)]) satisfy;
